      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0171",
      "sequence": 183,
      "meaning": "The false ascetic joyfully greets his friend and tells him the whole story. The demon says their enemy is already overcome if the sage follows his advice: he may rest free of care, for providence has cured the disease without medicine, uprooting the foe’s whole lineage; the demon will return on the fourth day. After greatly pleasing the pretender, the furious arch-deceiver instantly transports sleeping Pratāpabhānu and his horse home, lays the king beside his wife, and ties the horse neatly in its stable. He then abducts the royal priest, clouds his mind with illusion, and imprisons him in a mountain cave.",
