    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0172",
      "sequence": 184,
      "meaning": "Kālaketu assumes the priest’s appearance and lies on his fine bed. At an unsuspected dawn the king wakes in his palace, marvels at the feat, and silently goes home so even the queen does not know; later he rides the same horse to the forest without any citizen noticing. After six hours he returns amid celebrations. When he sees the seeming priest, he recalls the plan in amazement; the next three days feel like an age as his mind remains fixed on the false sage’s feet. At the appointed time the disguised priest comes, explains everything privately, and the delighted, deluded king recognizes him as his guru. He immediately invites one hundred thousand Brahmins with their families.",
