      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0173",
      "sequence": 185,
      "meaning": "The false priest prepares the feast with the six flavours and four kinds of food named by scripture. His illusory cooking includes countless dishes of many animals, among which the villain mixes Brahmin flesh. The king respectfully summons and seats all the Brahmins after washing their feet. Just as he begins serving, a heavenly voice warns them to rise, go home and eat none of the food, because Brahmin flesh has been cooked. Believing the voice, all rise. The bewildered king loses his judgment and cannot speak. Without reflection, the enraged Brahmins curse the foolish king and his entire family to become night-rangers.",
