    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0174",
      "sequence": 186,
      "meaning": "The Brahmins denounce Pratāpabhānu as a base ruler who invited the whole community in order to destroy it. God has preserved their dharma, but the king and his family will perish: within a year his line will be extinguished, with no descendant left to offer water. The terrified king hears the curse, then another heavenly voice declares that the Brahmins pronounced it without due thought because the king committed no offence. Astonished, they follow him to the dining place, where neither food nor Brahmins nor cook remains. The king returns in boundless grief, tells them everything and falls trembling to the ground. They reply that fate cannot be erased; though he is blameless, the dreadful Brahmin curse cannot be undone.",
