    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0175",
      "sequence": 187,
      "meaning": "The Brahmins depart and the townspeople, hearing the news, grieve and blame fate for turning a wandering swan into a crow. The demon returns the priest to his home and informs the false ascetic. The villain sends letters everywhere; enemy kings muster armies and rush upon Pratāpabhānu’s city, surround it with sounding drums, and wage battle day after day. All the king’s warriors fight bravely, but he and his brother fall, and no one of Satyaketu’s lineage survives—the Brahmin curse cannot prove false. Victorious enemies occupy the city and return home with fame. When the Creator turns hostile, dust becomes Mount Meru, a father becomes Death, and a rope becomes a serpent.",
